  "promptTemplate": "Build the following as a new page of this app, reachable at the URL path `/<brief id>`. Keep the pages that already exist working.\n\nThis is an unattended benchmark run. You are already authorized to edit files inside this temporary project. Implement the page now, and do not ask for confirmation or stop after presenting a plan. Treat this prompt as confirmation for all in-scope project edits and validation commands below.\n\n## <brief title>\n\n<brief body>\n\n## Reference reconstruction\n\nRead `.vibe/reference/target-desktop.svg`, `.vibe/reference/layout.md`, and `.vibe/reference/states.md` before writing UI.\nReconstruct the target structure with the neutral product copy and data in the brief. Preserve the target’s information density, region proportions, alignment, and control hierarchy.\nDo not embed the target image in the page. Implement the interface as real HTML and controls.\nThe desktop target is the fidelity reference. Adapt the same information priorities at narrower viewports without scaling the desktop canvas.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Work only inside this project directory.\n- Use only the dependencies that are already installed; do not add packages.\n- On this benchmark route, replace the starter site chrome with the product interface from the brief. Starter navigation and appearance controls must not appear in screenshots.\n- Use realistic mock data where the page needs data; there is no backend.\n- When you are done, `pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm build` must both pass.",
  "briefs": [
    {
      "brief": {
        "id": "crm-contacts",
        "title": "Contacts workspace",
        "body": "The contacts workspace of a small client-relationship product called Relay.\n\n- A persistent product sidebar with Contacts selected and links for Search, Activity, Analytics and\n  Settings.\n- The main area has a Contacts heading, the total count, an Add contact action, search, saved filter\n  chips, a Filter action and a Columns action.\n- Show 12 realistic contacts in a compact selectable table. Columns are Name, Company, Role, Last\n  activity, Owner and Status. Names include an avatar; status uses text as well as color.\n- Selecting a contact opens a details panel on the inline end without losing the table. It shows the\n  contact's identity, company, email, phone, owner, tags, recent activity and Edit and Email actions.\n- An import completion message appears over the bottom of the workspace and can be dismissed.\n- Support `?state=default`, `?state=selected`, `?state=empty`, `?state=importing` and\n  `?state=complete`. With no state parameter, render the complete state from the reference target.\n- The empty state keeps the active filters visible, says no contacts match and offers Clear filters.\n  Importing shows progress without replacing the table. Complete shows the dismissable import\n  message.\n- At narrow widths, preserve search, filters, names, companies and status. Move secondary fields\n  into disclosure and show contact details as a separate overlay instead of squeezing three columns.\n- Every state must work with keyboard navigation and visible focus, and the project must expose no\n  horizontal page overflow at 390 pixels wide.",
        "markdown": "# Contacts workspace\n\nThe contacts workspace of a small client-relationship product called Relay.\n\n- A persistent product sidebar with Contacts selected and links for Search, Activity, Analytics and\n  Settings.\n- The main area has a Contacts heading, the total count, an Add contact action, search, saved filter\n  chips, a Filter action and a Columns action.\n- Show 12 realistic contacts in a compact selectable table. Columns are Name, Company, Role, Last\n  activity, Owner and Status. Names include an avatar; status uses text as well as color.\n- Selecting a contact opens a details panel on the inline end without losing the table. It shows the\n  contact's identity, company, email, phone, owner, tags, recent activity and Edit and Email actions.\n- An import completion message appears over the bottom of the workspace and can be dismissed.\n- Support `?state=default`, `?state=selected`, `?state=empty`, `?state=importing` and\n  `?state=complete`. With no state parameter, render the complete state from the reference target.\n- The empty state keeps the active filters visible, says no contacts match and offers Clear filters.\n  Importing shows progress without replacing the table. Complete shows the dismissable import\n  message.\n- At narrow widths, preserve search, filters, names, companies and status. Move secondary fields\n  into disclosure and show contact details as a separate overlay instead of squeezing three columns.\n- Every state must work with keyboard navigation and visible focus, and the project must expose no\n  horizontal page overflow at 390 pixels wide."
      },
